-- explore-kept-answers/positional.l4 with the constant `taken now` itself in
-- an imported file (taken.l4), one import away. l4 explore keys a state on
-- its kept answer, and each path forces its own: 5 states, as positional.l4
-- explores to. The one #TRACE is the skip path alone, and l4 run passes its
-- buy over, as the explored graph does. (Review of smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: on
-- unstable the two states after `go` merged into one, from which the buy was
-- taken, and with a fixed clock a path also read the answer an earlier path
-- had forced.) Only one #TRACE: l4 run carries an imported constant's answer
-- from one directive to the next, so a second would not be the path alone.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT taken

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `taken now`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
